59,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I don't like Option C at all! Remember the stinky bin house? It'll just be a smelly trap in August! Option A sounds like too much waiting, and Option B sounds like a big adventure!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried about Option C too, especially with the high costs I found. Option B seems fair, but moving the point frequently might be stressful for some. Maybe Option A is more stable?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A is a disaster waiting to happen. We already know nobody wants to be the ""trash police,"" so we'll just end up with a rotating schedule of people ignoring their duties. It's a recipe for more resentment.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,I'm with Shunichi! Option A is basically a part-time job we're volunteering for. Who wants to wake up at dawn to babysit trash? No thanks! Option B is way more playful and keeps things moving.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option C is impractical due to the filing requirements and costs. Option A merely formalizes a burden. Option B is the only logical choice, provided we account for the frontages that cannot physically accommodate the point.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"If we do Option B, we can make sure the smell doesn't stay in one place for too long! It's like a traveling trash party, but without the party part. I vote for B!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"If we go with Option B, we can avoid the high initial costs of a structure and the stress of a strict schedule. As long as we're mindful of each other's space, it seems the most balanced.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Option B is the least likely to create a permanent villain or a permanent victim. It distributes the annoyance, which is the only way to keep this neighborhood from imploding. I'll vote for B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,B is definitely the winner here! It's the only one that doesn't sound like a chore or a construction project. Let's keep it light and keep it moving. I'm voting for B!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is the only arrangement that addresses the historical imbalance of the current location. While some frontages are narrow, we can adjust the rotation intervals to ensure the burden is shared logically. I vote for B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,Everyone agrees! I'm so happy we all picked the same one. It's way better than a stinky box or standing around forever. Let's make the traveling trash point happen!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,It really is a relief that we've found a solution we all agree on. I'm glad we can avoid those high costs and keep things fair for everyone's budget and space.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Don't get too carried away. We've just agreed to move the problem around in a circle. Still, it's better than a permanent grudge. I'll stick with B; at least it's a fair distribution of misery.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"Exactly! A fair distribution of misery is still better than one person doing all the work. Let's just make sure the rotation is automatic so nobody has to be the ""coordinator."" I'm definitely sticking with B!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,The consensus is clear. Option B is the only choice that prevents a permanent imbalance of burden. We will simply need to refine the rotation to account for the physical limitations of the narrower frontages. I vote for B.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! We all agree! I'm voting for Option B! Let's make sure we help each other move the bins so it's like a team effort. This is going to be great!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'm so glad we could reach a consensus that respects everyone's situation. I'll vote for Option B as well. Let's work together to make this a smooth and harmonious transition for all of us!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Since we've all reached a consensus, I'll make it official. Option B it is. Let's just hope that rotating the trash doesn't lead to rotating the arguments. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"B it is! Let's just keep it simple and automatic so it stays effortless for everyone. No coordinators, no stress, just a little rotation. I vote for Option B!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for Option B. It is the only solution that logically corrects the current inequality. We must now ensure the rotation schedule is adjusted to reflect the actual usable space of each frontage.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
